From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Add an in-process user driver for PS5.

A PS5 title runs Wine in its own process, with no explorer, no display
server and no driver dll. With WINE_PS5_USER_DRIVER (set for __PROSPERO__)
win32u carries its own user driver, installed by load_display_driver(),
and get_desktop_window() takes the server-created desktop (the service
path) instead of starting explorer.

The driver (ps5drv.c):
- reports one virtual monitor, 800x600 or WINE_PS5_DESKTOP=WxH, sizes the
  server's desktop window to it and publishes it once, so the server
  bounds the cursor by it even if the prefix holds another display config;
- gives each window a 32-bpp surface and composes the flushed pixels of
  visible top-level windows into one screen buffer, handed to
  pw_wine_present(), the title's single presentation sink; a window just
  shown is redrawn, since it may have painted before it had this surface;
- drains pw_wine_next_input() in ProcessEvents into hardware input (keys,
  absolute pointer in screen pixels, buttons), with pw_wine_input_fd()
  as each GUI thread's queue fd so idle threads are woken, and brings the
  newest window to the foreground when nothing is, as no window manager
  does it here.
The sink calls are found with dlsym: ntdll.prx exports them on PS5, and a
preloaded library provides them in a host build.
